1
00:06:02,727 --> 00:06:08,727
Four strangers become friends. Four friends become
heroes. On the road to Silverado.

2
00:12:05,454 --> 00:12:11,454
Silverado is a western, action film directed by Lawrence Kasdan.

3
00:18:08,181 --> 00:18:14,181
Four unwitting heroes cross paths on their journey
to the sleepy town of Silverado.

4
00:24:10,909 --> 00:24:16,909
Little do they know the town where their family and friends reside has
been taken over by a corrupt sheriff and a murderous posse.

5
00:30:13,636 --> 00:30:19,636
It's up to the sharp-shooting foursome to save the day, but first they have to
break each other out of jail, and learn who their real friends are.

6
00:36:16,363 --> 00:36:22,363
Paden, played by Kevin Kline.

7
00:42:19,090 --> 00:42:25,090
Emmett, played by Scott Glenn.

8
00:48:21,818 --> 00:48:27,818
Malachi 'Mal' Johnson, played by Danny Glover.

9
00:54:24,545 --> 00:54:30,545
Jake, played by Kevin Costner.

10
01:00:27,272 --> 01:00:33,272
Cobb, played by Brian Dennehy.

11
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Hannah, played by Rosanna Arquette.

12
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
Silverado is a 1985 American Western film that was produced and directed by
Lawrence Kasdan, and written by Kasdan and his brother Mark.

13
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
It stars Kevin Kline, Scott Glenn, Danny Glover, and Kevin Costner.

14
01:24:38,181 --> 01:24:44,181
The supporting cast features Brian Dennehy, Rosanna Arquette, John
Cleese, Jeff Goldblum, Lynne Whitfield, and Linda Hunt.

15
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The film was produced by Columbia Pictures and Delphi III Productions, and distributed to
theatres by Columbia, and by Sony Pictures Home Entertainment for home media.

16
01:36:43,636 --> 01:36:49,636
The original soundtrack, with a score composed by Bruce
Broughton, was released by Geffen Records.

17
01:42:46,363 --> 01:42:52,363
On November 12, 2005, an expanded two-disc version of the
score was released by the Intrada Records label.

18
01:48:49,090 --> 01:48:55,090
Silverado premiered in the United States on July 10, 1985.

19
01:54:51,818 --> 01:54:57,818
Through an 11-week run, the film was shown at 1,190 theaters at its
widest release, and grossed $32,192,570 at the box office.

20
02:00:54,545 --> 02:01:00,545
Generally met with positive critical reviews, it was nominated for Best
Sound and Best Original Score at the 58th Academy Awards.

21
02:06:57,272 --> 02:07:03,272
The film explores themes of gunslinger, sheriff, saloon, fight, new mexico.
